<title>FRANCE: Cr Lyonnais sees higher 96 banking income.</title>
<headline>Cr Lyonnais sees higher 96 banking income.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jean Peyrelevade, chairman of state-owned bank Credit Lyonnais, said on Friday he expected the troubled bank to produce higher net banking income in 1996 despite a drop in banking income produced in France.</p>
<p>Peyrelevade also said he hoped French 1997 net banking income would stabilise in 1997 and grow in 1998.</p>
<p>Peyrelevade, speaking at a luncheon, gave no specific figures with his forecasts.</p>
</text>
